      "documentConcept": "Adaptive closed-loop DBS and directional leads",
      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:89953b47f37ba077998f30b256b6d0386a949880d3073e4ed98943f3033f8574",
      "text": "Adaptive DBS uses neural feedback to adjust stimulation; directional leads steer the stimulation field. These approaches address different programming dimensions. Personalized adaptive DBS showed benefits in a small feasibility trial, while another small beta-feedback trial found no significant advantage over continuous DBS. ADAPT-PD supported long-term tolerability and preserved therapeutic performance with important open-label design limits. Directional stimulation widened the therapeutic window in a randomized crossover study, but a separate randomized trial did not demonstrate superior motor outcomes. Algorithm, biomarker, endpoint, and programming differences matter when interpreting results.",
